Recurrent architectures, such as LSTM10 and GRU11, have gained widespread use for predicting pollutant time-series due to their ability to effectively learn temporal dependencies. To better capture local patterns and short-term dynamics, researchers have begun integrating convolutional layers with recurrent layers, which has led to enhanced accuracy in various urban and regional case studies. For example, CNN-LSTM10 and its variants32–34 have been successfully applied to city-scale PM\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
