				\begin{document}$$\le$$\end{document} 3 timesteps) are interpolated; longer gaps are masked and imputed using a small MLP imputer trained on neighboring cells. For sensors with persistently high missing ratios, spatial–correlation–based reconstruction is applied using adjacency-weighted estimates from nearby sensors within the same subgrid.
Spatial mapping: sensors are mapped to grid cells (Section on Spatial Grid Embedding) and aggregated per cell as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
